\label{cor:shifted-imaginary}
Let \(\varepsilon>0\) be fixed. Then, for fixed \(d\in\mathbb R\),
\[
\frac{1}{N(T)}
\sum_{0<\gamma<T}
\Im_{1-\varepsilon}\!\left(
\gamma-\frac{2\pi d}{\log T}
\right)
\sim
\int_0^1
2u(1-u)\sin(2\pi du)\,du.
\]
Equivalently, writing \(\alpha=2\pi d\),
\[
\frac{1}{N(T)}
\sum_{0<\gamma<T}
\Im_{1-\varepsilon}\!\left(
\gamma-\frac{\alpha}{\log T}
\right)
\sim
\frac{2\bigl(2-2\cos\alpha-\alpha\sin\alpha\bigr)}
{\alpha^3}.
\]
